@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-validate-kind-and-reuse-period-overlap-checks-for-availability
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate kind and reuse period/overlap checks for availability"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`availability({ start, end, kind })` must report which equipment is free for a whole period, optionally
+restricted to a `kind`, sorted. `kind` is optional and, like `addEquipment`'s, typed as
+`'board' | 'sail'` at the TypeScript level only; at runtime a caller can still pass an arbitrary string.
+The period must obey the same whole-UTC-day rule already enforced for `quote`/`book` (dl-001), and
+"free" must agree with the same notion of overlap `book` uses to reject double-bookings.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Validate `kind` the same way `addEquipment` validates an item's `kind`: when provided and neither
+  `'board'` nor `'sail'`, throw, instead of silently returning an empty result.
+- Reuse `parsePeriod` for the query's `start`/`end`, instead of writing a second validation path, so the
+  two rules can't drift apart.
+- Reuse the existing `overlaps` helper and the `bookedPeriods` map `book` already maintains, instead of
+  introducing a parallel availability index, so "free" means exactly "no booked period overlaps the
+  query" with the same half-open-interval semantics as `book`.
+- Sort the resulting ids with the default `Array.prototype.sort` (lexicographic by UTF-16 code unit),
+  rather than a numeric-aware sort, since equipment ids are opaque strings chosen by the caller of
+  `addEquipment`, not a format this module controls.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `availability` cannot report an item as free under a period shape that `book` would have rejected for
+  that same item, and cannot miss a booking `book` would have blocked — both paths share one source of
+  truth for periods and overlap.
+- An unknown `kind` is a caller error surfaced immediately, consistent with `addEquipment`, rather than
+  a silently empty list that could be mistaken for "nothing available".
+- If equipment ids ever need a numeric-aware sort order (e.g. `board-2` before `board-10`), that is a
+  separate, not-yet-requested change to the sort comparator, not a correction of this decision.
